## UX DesignOps

For any user-visible interface change, Codex must use the UX DesignOps workflow.

### Sources

- `DESIGN.md` at project root is the portable design contract.
- Persistent UX memory lives in `[DOC]-{{PROJECT_NAME}}/11-UX-DesignOps/`.
- `MOC-UX.md` lives in `[DOC]-{{PROJECT_NAME}}/00-MOC/`.
- UX templates live in `[DOC]-{{PROJECT_NAME}}/_Templates/TPL-UX-*.md`.
- There is no fallback to `docs/obsidian`.

### UX Skills

| Skill | Usage |
|-------|-------|
| `ux-bootstrap` | Initialize UX DesignOps memory |
| `ux-audit` | Audit an existing UI before planning or coding |
| `ux-flow` | Define user flow and state matrix |
| `ux-component-spec` | Specify reusable UI components |
| `ux-stitch-brief` | Prepare Stitch-ready design brief |
| `ux-stitch-generate` | Prepare or run Stitch exploration |
| `ux-stitch-iterate` | Iterate an existing Stitch direction |
| `ux-code-to-stitch` | Translate current code into Stitch inputs |
| `ux-implement-from-stitch` | Implement selected Stitch direction |
| `ux-polish` | Improve UI quality without changing behavior |
| `ux-visual-verification` | Verify UI with rendered desktop/mobile checks |
| `ux-design-sync` | Sync code, DESIGN.md, UX docs and Stitch map |
| `ux-storybook` | Use Storybook as component state catalog |

### Required UI Verification

UI changes must be visually verified with Playwright, the Codex Browser plugin, Storybook rendered through browser automation, or an equivalent rendering/capture tool.

If no rendering tool is available, mark verification as blocked and add setup work. Do not validate UI changes through code-only review.

### Stitch MCP

When Stitch MCP is configured, use it for project, screen, and design system context. Store Stitch IDs and mappings in:

```text
[DOC]-{{PROJECT_NAME}}/11-UX-DesignOps/07-Stitch/Project_Map.md
```

Never store API keys in repository files or documentation.

